{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass.\n\nThe fix in `repo/stats.py` replaces the buggy truncated rank with the proper nearest-rank method:\n\n```python\nrank = -(-p * n // 100)  # ceiling division\nif rank < 1:\n    rank = 1\nreturn ordered[rank - 1]\n```\n\n- **Was:** `idx = int(p / 100 * n)` — truncation gives a rank one too high (e.g. p=50 of 10 values → idx 5 → value 6) and crashes with `IndexError` at p=100 (idx 10).\n- **Now:** `rank = ceil(p / 100 * n)`, clamped to `[1, n]`, then `ordered[rank - 1]`. So p=0 → min, p=100 → max, and p=50 of 1..10 → 5."}]},"session_id":"8a7e8807-d1ac-4a70-9062-91b5c25dbe42"}
